{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash32-compat","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"Shell-heavy telemetry changes need focused review for macOS Bash 3.2 portability and safe best-effort behavior.","prompt_body":"Inspect the new and modified shell scripts for Bash 3.2 compatibility, quoting, arithmetic edge cases, and trap/tempfile behavior. Pay special attention to helper scripts that canonicalize tmpdirs, parse env/json-like files, or append ledger rows while swallowing telemetry failures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ledger-schema","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff introduces a new 13-column timing-ledger row type consumed by JSON rendering and tests.","prompt_body":"Verify that every producer of timing round rows writes exactly the schema planned and that every consumer parses the same field positions. Check validation, duration clamping, optional oos handling, idempotency, and backward compatibility for existing mark/report behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"interval-attachment","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Round rows must attach only to matching step intervals, including resumed Step 5 and nested design intervals.","prompt_body":"Review the timing-report aggregation logic for exact skill, step label, and interval matching. Look for off-by-one interval mistakes, nested child-step attachment bugs, ordering/sorting issues, or cases where resumed Step 5 rounds could attach to Step 7 or an earlier interval. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"handoff-telemetry","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Main-agent-vote and coder-main-agent handoffs defer round telemetry across prompt-side work and wrapper resumes.","prompt_body":"Trace the implement and design handoff paths where round starts are persisted and telemetry is emitted later. Check that MAV re-tallying, prompt-side checks/lint, stall exits, and successful resume paths all record one correct row without stretching duration past commit or publish phases. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-publish","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Design log publishing changes risk stale timing artifacts or unintended sidecars leaking into committed run logs.","prompt_body":"Examine design timing render and publish changes for stale artifact removal, atomic JSON publication, excluded stderr/failure sidecars, and allowlist consistency. Verify that failed renders leave no publishable timing-report-final siblings and that round-start-s survives only where needed. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"count-parsing","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Accepted, rejected, and OOS counts come from heterogeneous markdown, env, and tally artifacts with subtle formats.","prompt_body":"Review helper parsing for accepted findings, rejected compact rows with optional grep prefixes, plan-review rejected headings, round-local tally precedence, and accepted-only OOS rows. Look for regex mismatches, fallback ordering problems, zero-count handling, or accidental counts from stale or wrong-scope files. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
